Decisions not in the request: `flush()` is a no-op when nothing is pending (rather than calling `fn` with no args); `cancel()` also clears stored args so a later `flush()` can't resurrect a cancelled call; timer firing clears stored args; negative-ms error message is `ms must be >= 0, got ${ms}`.

